Hi Filipe,

I am working on developing an algorithm for wheat ear count detection from drone imagery. The resolution of our images is 0.19 cm/pixel. Reference reprints followed were Zhao et al., 2021 (https://doi.org/10.3390/rs13163095) and Zhan et al., 2022 (https://doi.org/10.1007/s00500-021-06407-8 ).

We have annotated 5 drone images to see the detection. Each image has approx.5k annotations. We were using Model: Yolov5 , (s , m, l ,x ,5v6 ,5s6, 5m6 ,5l6, 5x6 ) and yolox. But detection of the wheat ear was a challenge. I would like to get some suggestions for better detection especially for feature extraction architecture (backbone) in wheat ears through any online platforms.

Kindly suggest the techniques for feature extraction of the wheat ear.

Thank you,
Sudhir.

